{"belief_id":"blf_loss_dominated_by_rare_tokens_2000","created_at":"2026-07-22T02:15:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-campaign","evidence_ids":[],"fingerprint":"0d107e19d8cfb08e","limitations":["Single seed; screen-level (no formal RunRecord for the diagnostic run). Capacity-vs-compute confound unresolved -- the whole model is underfit, so rare-token loss may be undertraining rather than capacity-limited."],"next_test":"Resolve capacity-vs-compute: (a) DIAGNOSE at two budgets (1000 vs 2000) -- if rare-token loss still dropping steeply, it's compute-limited; (b) if plateauing, a gated strong-form n-gram-capacity experiment (min_effect from the rare-token loss mass, >= 2x floor) via run_gated.","rationale":"DIAGNOSE=1 per-token decomposition over the val stream.","scope":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"},"statement":"Mechanistic diagnosis (DIAGNOSE per-token decomposition, baseline seed42): val loss is DOMINATED BY RARE TOKENS and roughly FLAT across sequence position. Mean per-token nats rise monotonically from common to rare (freq deciles: 1.37/1.67/1.89/2.10/2.60/2.63/3.08/3.32/3.66/3.76); the rare 40% of tokens (d6-d9) carry ~3.45 nats vs ~1.6 for the common head. Position bins are ~flat (2.52-2.77, no gradient after ~512). => the bottleneck is the vocab/frequency tail, NOT context length. This localizes the one untried structural axis (n-gram / vocab-tail capacity) and gives it a predicted effect size; it does NOT by itself resolve whether the rare-token loss is capacity-limited (enrichment helps) or compute-limited (more steps needed, enrichment won't help at fixed budget).","status":"supported","subject_ids":["mech_ngram_short_context_memory","clm_r2_ngram_scone_scaling_embeddings_3"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["mechanistic","rare_tokens","vocab_tail","diagnosis","differentiator"],"version":1}
{"belief_id":"blf_compute_limited_fair_space_exhausted_2000","created_at":"2026-07-22T02:45:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-campaign","evidence_ids":[],"fingerprint":"67f6fd019b446a27","limitations":["Screen-level (diagnostic runs not formal RunRecords). Conclusion scoped to the FAIR frame (frozen data/compute/eval); it explicitly does NOT say the model is optimal -- more compute or a relaxed frame would help, but those are outside the fair-game rules."],"next_test":"None within the fair frame -- it is exhausted. Value now is the map + integrity infrastructure, not a delta. Any further gain requires renegotiating the frozen axes (more steps/compute) with the operator.","rationale":"DIAGNOSE per-decile loss at two budgets + adversarial verification of the capacity-vs-compute inference.","scope":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"},"statement":"DEFINITIVE (DIAGNOSE 1000 vs 2000 steps, verified): the 2000-step nanoGPT baseline is COMPUTE-LIMITED on every fair axis, not method-limited. Per-token loss drops faster on the RARE tail than the common head from 1000->2000 (d9 -6.5%, d6 -6.0%, d3 -5.2%, d0 -4.6%) -> the rare tokens where loss concentrates are being ACTIVELY LEARNED, not plateaued/capacity-limited. val_bpb 1000->2000 = 0.986->0.930 (-0.056, ~80x the 0.000847 floor). By the verification decision rule (differential plateau REQUIRED to license a capacity bet; observed the opposite), the strong-form n-gram / vocab-tail structural bet is KILLED. Combined with: n-gram tables already at 64x (prior crossover win), n-gram-LR null, and every knob screen sub-floor -> the FAIR search space is genuinely exhausted. The binding constraint is COMPUTE (frozen by the fair-game rules). No fair lever (knob or structural) clears the floor at this budget.","status":"strongly_supported","subject_ids":["mech_ngram_short_context_memory","clm_scaling_data_constrained_1"],"supersedes_belief_id":"blf_loss_dominated_by_rare_tokens_2000","tags":["compute_limited","fair_space_exhausted","definitive","mechanistic","differentiator"],"version":1}
