{"belief_id":"blf_underfit_regime_2000_spec","created_at":"2026-07-22T06:05:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":[],"fingerprint":"49c38e53e09c2c8b","limitations":["Screen-level evidence: raw per-step artifacts in remote logs + ongoing_experiment notes; no formal RunRecord/EvidenceRecord (appears in current_belief_without_evidence audit warning by design).","2026-07-22: revised to speculative -- prior-session assertion with no structured evidence registered in this ledger; treat as an unconfirmed prior until run evidence is linked."],"next_test":"If a convergence-speed lever (e.g. DOC_MASK) clears the 0.0007 floor, confirm the mechanism is per-step-quality (not regularization) via the val-loss trajectory.","rationale":"Observable-driven regime diagnosis from per-step val_loss vs progress across the epoch boundary; monotone decrease + flat gap => underfit.","scope":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"},"statement":"At the 2000-step frozen challenge (rsi/daniel baseline, shards 1-10), the model is UNDERFIT/compute-limited, not overfitting the repeated data: smoothed val_loss decreases monotonically to the budget end (-0.15 nats over the last 40%, 3 runs/2 seeds) and the train-val gap stays flat ~0 across the 1.6-epoch boundary. Therefore anti-repetition regularization (focal reweighting, dropout, weight-decay increases) is the wrong direction, and the productive axis is convergence-speed (make each fixed step more effective), not capacity or regularization.","status":"speculative","subject_ids":["clm_scaling_data_constrained_1","clm_base_recipes_cramming_2"],"supersedes_belief_id":"blf_underfit_regime_2000","tags":["regime","underfit","repeated_data","regularization_wrong_direction","mechanistic","priority"],"version":2}
