{"belief_id":"blf_ngram_capacity_decomposition","created_at":"2026-07-22T09:15:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_ngram_bigram_256_discovery","evd_run_ngram_trigram_256_discovery"],"fingerprint":"d96716eac24153c9","limitations":["only the 256x level probed per type; the bigram/trigram capacity ratio was not swept"],"next_test":"If pushing further, sweep the bigram:trigram capacity ratio under a fixed VRAM budget to find the efficient allocation.","rationale":"Two matched-seed 3-seed discoveries decompose the confirmed both-256x win; sub-additivity indicates partial redundancy between bigram and trigram hashed memories.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"repeated-data 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"The 256x n-gram capacity win (-0.00405) is split roughly evenly across BOTH n-gram orders: bigram-only 256x gives -0.00236 (t=-22), trigram-only 256x gives -0.00249 (t=-15), each individually floor-clearing. Sum -0.00485 = 120% of the combined effect -> SUB-ADDITIVE (~20% of the rare-ngram signal is redundant across orders). No single table drives the win; scaling both is (weakly) better than either alone.","status":"strongly_supported","subject_ids":["hyp_ngram_bigram_256","hyp_ngram_trigram_256","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["ngram","capacity","decomposition"],"version":1}
{"belief_id":"blf_ngram_capacity_frontier_diminishing","created_at":"2026-07-22T10:25:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_ngram_bigram_512_discovery","evd_run_ngram_capacity_128_discovery"],"fingerprint":"76d65f352bdced8d","limitations":["2000-step scope; asymmetric bigram:trigram ratio under fixed VRAM not exhaustively swept"],"next_test":"Capacity axis is exhausted for adoption; pursue a different subsystem (loss shaping / data order / architecture).","rationale":"Frontier probe at 512x confirms diminishing sub-floor marginal returns; capacity axis is mined out at the practical 256x operating point.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"repeated-data 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"n-gram capacity keeps improving monotonically to the VRAM ceiling but with sub-floor marginal returns past 256x: bigram 512x gives -0.00302 vs baseline (t=-26), only -0.00066 more than bigram-256x. Combined with the 128->256 sub-floor increment and sub-additive bigram/trigram decomposition, the capacity axis is practically saturated at 256x; further scaling is not worth the VRAM (512x ~132GB near the 143GB ceiling).","status":"strongly_supported","subject_ids":["hyp_ngram_bigram_512","hyp_ngram_capacity_256","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["ngram","capacity","frontier","saturation"],"version":1}
{"belief_id":"blf_data_order_small_real_subfloor","created_at":"2026-07-22T03:40:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_shuffle_data_discovery"],"fingerprint":"5e5c24bb8e9e8327","limitations":["only plain reshuffle tested; curriculum/packing/difficulty-ordering not tried","effect may grow with more epochs"],"next_test":"If revisiting data-order, try a difficulty-ordered curriculum or best-fit packing (needs a lib.py policy); otherwise pivot axis.","rationale":"3-seed discovery: directionally real, sub-floor. Order matters but weakly at this horizon.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"repeated-data 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"Data presentation order has a small but real effect in this constrained ~1.6-epoch regime: reshuffle-between-epochs (SHUFFLE_DATA) lowers 2000-step val_bpb by mean -0.00094 (3/3 seeds, paired-t -3.0), above the 1x seed floor but BELOW the 2x adoption floor (0.001694). Data order is not irrelevant here (consistent with 'curriculum helps in constrained regimes'), but plain reshuffle is not adopt-grade at 1.6 epochs; a stronger policy (curriculum/packing) or more epochs would be needed to clear the floor.","status":"supported","subject_ids":["hyp_shuffle_data_decorrelation","mech_data_order_constrained","clm_data_when_do_curricula_work_2"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["data_order","sub_floor"],"version":1}
