{"belief_id":"blf_ngram_order_redundant_with_capacity","created_at":"2026-07-22T06:45:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_ngram128_fourgram","evd_run_ngram_fourgram_pilot"],"fingerprint":"33a18bcc61baa73e","limitations":["only 4gram@256x on 128x tested"],"next_test":"N-gram family exhausted for SOTA gains; different subsystem needed.","rationale":"128x+4gram ties 256x; order substitutes for capacity rather than adding.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"repeated-data 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"N-gram ORDER (4-gram) and hash-bucket CAPACITY are largely REDUNDANT, not orthogonal: 128x+4gram ties the 256x SOTA (mean -0.000343 vs 256x, t=-1.18, ns). Both mechanisms encode the same rare-ngram information, so combining them does not add. The 256x capacity win (0.9253) is not improved by adding 4-gram order. Consistent with the sub-additive bigram/trigram decomposition.","status":"strongly_supported","subject_ids":["hyp_ngram128_plus_fourgram","hyp_ngram_fourgram","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["ngram","order","capacity","redundant"],"version":1}
