{"belief_id":"blf_pk_memory_fails_at_this_budget","created_at":"2026-07-22T22:50:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_pk_memory_default","evd_run_pk_memory_lr025"],"fingerprint":"eaf9c0d1f49598e3","limitations":["2 LR points","budget-vs-architecture confound is not resolvable within the frozen challenge"],"next_test":"Secondary bets (doc-local recurrent/summary memory; collision-aware multi-hash routing; sparse residual experts) OR accept that added-capacity architectures do not pay off at 2000 steps.","rationale":"Both arms fail the pre-registered threshold; LR trend explains the harm but not a benefit.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"single-pass ~0.47 epoch 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"The primary architecture bet -- a learned product-key sparse memory (4.84B params, 4.19M slots/layer on layers [1,5,7], top-16 retrieval, zero-init gate giving exact step-0 identity with the SOTA) -- FAILS at this compute budget. Default router LR: +0.000593 (3/3 seeds worse, t=+2.56). Router LR x0.25: -0.000138 (mixed, t=-0.67, null). Neither meets the -0.001 advance threshold. The router LR is highly influential (a 4x reduction moved the result -0.000731), confirming the pre-flagged thrash mechanism, but the best case is INERT rather than helpful. HONEST AMBIGUITY: this cannot distinguish 'learned retrieval does not beat random hashing for this model' from '2000 steps is too short for a zero-initialised 4.84B-param memory to learn any useful routing' -- the value table starts at zero, so the memory must learn what to store AND how to route before it can pay for itself. Testing that distinction requires a longer budget, which the frozen challenge forbids.","status":"supported","subject_ids":["hyp_pk_memory","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["pk_memory","retrieval","architecture","negative"],"version":1}
{"belief_id":"blf_fourgram_helps_on_fixed_code","created_at":"2026-07-22T23:35:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_fourgram_remeasure","evd_run_fourgram_gate_bug"],"fingerprint":"2757486ae3d81471","limitations":["discovery seeds only","below 2-sigma floor"],"next_test":"Hold-out validation on seeds 46-51; if it holds, this is a new SOTA component.","rationale":"3/3 negative, t=-4.63, passes advance threshold on trustworthy code.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"single-pass ~0.47 epoch 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"4-gram value embeddings @256x DO help: -0.001206 vs the SOTA (3/3 seeds, paired-t=-4.63), passing the -0.001 funnel threshold. This REVERSES the retracted conclusion that n-gram order is redundant with capacity -- that was a false negative from the uninitialized fourgram_gate. 4th-order context carries real predictive information beyond bigram+trigram in this regime. Two enabling facts: (a) the gate bug had to be fixed for the signal to be measurable at all; (b) the configuration was previously OOM-blocked at ~151GB and became runnable only via the rowwise-state and sparse-gradient infrastructure (76.6GB peak). Hold-out validation on seeds 46-51 required before adoption.","status":"supported","subject_ids":["hyp_fourgram_remeasure","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["ngram","fourgram","order","win","reversal"],"version":1}
{"belief_id":"blf_sota_004_fourgram","created_at":"2026-07-23T00:15:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_fourgram_holdout","evd_run_fourgram_remeasure"],"fingerprint":"c1fade13be986bd2","limitations":["increment below the 2-sigma per-experiment floor"],"next_test":"Does the ORDER ladder continue (5-gram)? Is 4-gram capacity saturating (128/256/384 sweep)?","rationale":"6/6 hold-out seeds, t=-26.27, replicates discovery.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"single-pass ~0.47 epoch 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"SOTA #4: 256x n-gram capacity + intra-document seg attention mask + WARMDOWN_RATIO=0.75 + 4-gram VE @256x -> hold-out val_bpb 0.922710 (6 seeds 46-51), -0.000973 below the prior SOTA and -0.007937 below the frozen baseline 0.930647. The 4-gram increment is -0.001307 (6/6 seeds, paired-t=-26.27, p<0.01). NOTE ON PROVENANCE: this axis had been RETRACTED as a false negative -- fourgram_gate was never initialized under meta+to_empty, so the 4-gram signal was injected through a random gate, producing the wrong conclusion that 'order is redundant with capacity'. Fixing the gate reversed it. The configuration ALSO required the rowwise-state and sparse-gradient infrastructure, since it previously OOM'd at ~151GB and now runs at 76.6GB. Four orthogonal additive components now: capacity, attention masking, LR schedule, n-gram ORDER.","status":"strongly_supported","subject_ids":["hyp_fourgram_remeasure","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"blf_sota_final_converged","tags":["sota","fourgram","order","best_config"],"version":1}
{"belief_id":"blf_fourgram_capacity_knee_at_256","created_at":"2026-07-23T01:00:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_fourgram_capacity_sweep","evd_run_ngram384_capacity"],"fingerprint":"7a8963db90f3d226","limitations":["3 seeds per arm","only 128/256/384 sampled"],"next_test":"Order ladder (5-gram) requires new code -- see gap_no_fivegram_order_lever. Or base-capacity x 4-gram interaction.","rationale":"384x null, 128x consistently worse; matches the base-capacity saturation point.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"single-pass ~0.47 epoch 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"The 4-gram ORDER has the same capacity knee as the base n-gram tables: 256x. Going UP to 384x is null (mean -0.000294, mixed sign, t=-1.31, fails the -0.001 funnel); going DOWN to 128x is consistently worse (+0.000407, 3/3 seeds, t=4.19), so the capacity is genuinely used and cannot be reclaimed. This mirrors the base bigram/trigram capacity axis, which also saturated between 256x and 384x (-0.000611, sub-threshold). Coherent picture: hash-bucket capacity pays up to ~256x and then stops, INDEPENDENT of n-gram order -- the order axis adds information (4-gram gave -0.001307) but does not shift where capacity saturates.","status":"supported","subject_ids":["hyp_fourgram_capacity_sweep","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["ngram","fourgram","capacity","knee","saturating"],"version":1}
{"belief_id":"blf_capacity_and_order_are_separable","created_at":"2026-07-23T01:35:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_ids":["evd_run_base_capacity_x_fourgram","evd_run_fourgram_capacity_sweep","evd_run_fourgram_holdout"],"fingerprint":"efd00397ebc804a9","limitations":["3 seeds","cross-config comparison for the interaction sign"],"next_test":"5-gram: does the ORDER ladder continue past 4-gram? (EXPLORE:NGRAM_FIVEGRAM now implemented.)","rationale":"Base-capacity effect essentially unchanged by the presence of 4-gram; each order saturates at 256x.","scope":{"model":"nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8","regime":"single-pass ~0.47 epoch 2000-step H200","scope_key":{"data_split_sha256":"ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3","max_steps":2000,"outcome_id":"out_val_bpb","stop_mode":"steps"}},"statement":"N-gram CAPACITY and n-gram ORDER are separable, independent axes. (1) Base capacity 256->384 is sub-threshold both WITHOUT 4-gram (-0.000611) and WITH it (-0.000240, t=-2.43, fails the -0.001 gate) -- adding the order does not make extra base capacity worth more. (2) The 4-gram order has its own capacity knee also at 256x (384x null, 128x worse 3/3). (3) The order axis itself paid substantially (4-gram -0.001307, 6/6 hold-out seeds). So: capacity buys you up to ~256x per order and then stops, while ORDER adds genuinely new information on top. This is why the SOTA path was capacity-first then order, not capacity-only.","status":"supported","subject_ids":["hyp_base_capacity_x_fourgram","mech_ngram_short_context_memory"],"supersedes_belief_id":"","tags":["ngram","capacity","order","separable","saturating"],"version":1}
{"belief_id": "blf_ngram_order_ladder_terminates_at_fourgram", "created_at": "2026-07-23T02:05:00-07:00", "created_by": "claude-ledger", "evidence_ids": ["evd_run_fivegram_order", "evd_run_fourgram_holdout", "evd_run_fourgram_capacity_sweep"], "fingerprint": "1982e1f056510068", "limitations": ["3 seeds", "cannot separate absent signal from unlearnable signal at this token budget"], "next_test": "Retest the 5-gram rung first if the step/token budget is ever unfrozen; nothing further on this axis at 2000 steps.", "rationale": "Per-rung marginal effect decays ~2.8x from 4-gram to 5-gram and falls below both the advance gate and the seed floor.", "scope": {"model": "nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8", "regime": "single-pass ~0.47 epoch 2000-step H200", "scope_key": {"data_split_sha256": "ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3", "max_steps": 2000, "outcome_id": "out_val_bpb", "stop_mode": "steps"}}, "statement": "The n-gram ORDER ladder terminates at 4-gram in this regime. Marginal gain per rung decays sharply: bigram+trigram (baseline config) -> 4-gram -0.001307 (adopted, 6/6 hold-out seeds) -> 5-gram -0.000470 (2/3 seeds, t=-1.92, fails the -0.001 gate, below the 2-sigma floor). Combined with [[blf_capacity_and_order_are_separable]] -- which closed the capacity axis at 256x on every rung -- BOTH dimensions of the n-gram value-embedding design space are now mapped: capacity saturates at 256x per order, and order saturates at 4. IMPORTANT SCOPE LIMIT: the 5-gram point estimate is negative (helping), just too small to clear the gate. The honest claim is 'not worth its cost at 2000 steps / 294.9M tokens', NOT '5th-order context is useless'. At this budget most distinct 5-grams occur once or never, so the rung is plausibly data-starved rather than information-free -- it is the natural first thing to retest if the step or token budget is ever unfrozen.", "status": "supported", "subject_ids": ["hyp_fivegram_order", "mech_ngram_short_context_memory"], "supersedes_belief_id": "", "tags": ["ngram", "order", "saturating", "closed_axis", "data_budget_limit"], "version": 1}
{"belief_id": "blf_fourgram_win_is_shape_robust", "created_at": "2026-07-23T03:55:00-07:00", "created_by": "claude-ledger", "evidence_ids": ["evd_run_gappy_fourgram_dose", "evd_run_fourgram_holdout"], "fingerprint": "5f8360a960a9d1fa", "limitations": ["3 seeds", "decides only the extreme branch of the intended contrast", "reused controls"], "next_test": "A better-powered (6+ seed) sweep over several gappy shapes at graded singleton rates would resolve whether singleton rate mediates the order ceiling; not worth the GPU time inside the frozen scope.", "rationale": "Null delta with a CI that excludes the range-decay magnitude but not zero or the sparsity prediction.", "scope": {"model": "nanoGPT rsi/daniel n_layer=8", "regime": "single-pass ~0.47 epoch 2000-step H200", "scope_key": {"data_split_sha256": "ed8ea0554010df9fbfa47746adc6643d6446797753eb377c0b35413bdcf2fca3", "max_steps": 2000, "outcome_id": "out_val_bpb", "stop_mode": "steps"}}, "statement": "The 4-gram value-embedding win does NOT depend on the contiguity of its context window. Replacing the contiguous shape (w[-3],w[-2],w[-1],w[0]) with the gappy shape (w[-4],w[-2],w[-1],w[0]) is NULL (+0.000139, t=+0.82, 95% CI [-0.000589,+0.000867]) even though the gappy context is measurably sparser (60.3% vs 45.8% singleton rate). The strong RANGE-DECAY hypothesis -- that the adjacent position w[-3] carries information w[-4] cannot replace -- is EXCLUDED, since that would have cost ~+0.0012, outside the CI. So what the 4-gram rung buys is the EXISTENCE of a 4-token conjunction, not its adjacency structure. SCOPE LIMIT, stated deliberately: this experiment was designed to discriminate sparsity-mediation from range-decay and only decided the range-decay branch. The CI contains both zero and the pure-sparsity prediction, so [[blf_ngram_order_ladder_terminates_at_fourgram]]'s data-budget explanation is NOT confirmed here. It is mildly challenged: the per-singleton-point slope implied by this arm is 3.2x shallower than the one implied by the 4->5-gram step, which would suggest singleton rate alone is insufficient to explain the order ceiling -- but that slope is itself not resolved from zero at 3 seeds.", "status": "supported", "subject_ids": ["hyp_gappy_fourgram_sparsity_dose", "mech_ngram_short_context_memory"], "supersedes_belief_id": "", "tags": ["ngram", "fourgram", "context_shape", "null", "scope_limit"], "version": 1}
